1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Last time, you wrote one quest,

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:04,772
and a quest is a task.

3
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:08,779
This is a story, with a beginning, a middle,

4
00:00:09,229 --> 00:00:11,843
and an ending you can win or lose.

5
00:00:12,743 --> 00:00:16,184
It's still one text file, and it's still no code.

6
00:00:17,084 --> 00:00:19,367
And the quest you wrote last time

7
00:00:19,817 --> 00:00:22,013
is going to be its first step.

8
00:00:23,813 --> 00:00:25,957
Here's how a story looks in the Quest Log.

9
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:29,080
Salvage Run is a heading in the list,

10
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:30,866
with its steps under it,

11
00:00:31,316 --> 00:00:33,973
and a clock under its name counting down.

12
00:00:34,873 --> 00:00:37,611
Select it, and its own briefing is on the right,

13
00:00:38,061 --> 00:00:39,680
with a small table in the middle.

14
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:44,228
A story needs a heading in the file too,

15
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:46,971
and it's made the way every heading is:

16
00:00:47,421 --> 00:00:49,835
three hashes, a name, and a key.

17
00:00:50,735 --> 00:00:54,754
Inside the fence there's one word on a line by itself,

18
00:00:55,204 --> 00:00:57,624
the word Arc, with no colon after it.

19
00:00:58,524 --> 00:00:59,988
What that word says is,

20
00:01:00,438 --> 00:01:03,454
I'm not a task, I'm the heading over some tasks.

21
00:01:05,254 --> 00:01:06,631
The rest you've seen before:

22
00:01:07,081 --> 00:01:09,390
it's shared, and it starts at once.

23
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:11,998
Below the fence comes the briefing,

24
00:01:12,448 --> 00:01:15,454
and this time it has a table of what DS 1 knows.

25
00:01:16,354 --> 00:01:19,374
Every line of a table starts and ends with a bar,

26
00:01:19,824 --> 00:01:22,933
and the second line is just bars and hyphens.

27
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:26,189
Then one more line, for what's at stake.

28
00:01:27,089 --> 00:01:29,739
And that's all of what the Quest Log shows

29
00:01:30,189 --> 00:01:32,388
when the crew selects Salvage Run.

30
00:01:33,588 --> 00:01:36,589
Now for the trick, and it's just one more hash.

31
00:01:37,489 --> 00:01:42,274
Four hashes means, I'm a step of the three-hash record above me.

32
00:01:43,174 --> 00:01:44,825
And that's all nesting is.

33
00:01:46,625 --> 00:01:48,899
So Close Inspection was a quest,

34
00:01:49,349 --> 00:01:52,409
and now it's step one of Salvage Run.

35
00:01:53,309 --> 00:01:56,999
In the Quest Log, it's listed under Salvage Run now,

36
00:01:57,449 --> 00:01:59,283
and not on a line of its own.

37
00:02:00,183 --> 00:02:05,653
And in the file it has a full address: salvage, slash, approach.

38
00:02:06,853 --> 00:02:09,654
Step two goes here, and not at the bottom of the section.

39
00:02:10,554 --> 00:02:15,614
That's because a four-hash step belongs to the nearest three-hash heading above it,

40
00:02:16,064 --> 00:02:19,417
and my quest from last time is a three-hash heading.

41
00:02:20,317 --> 00:02:21,534
So if I type below it,

42
00:02:21,984 --> 00:02:24,354
my new step joins the wrong story,

43
00:02:24,804 --> 00:02:27,141
and the game is won at the first step.

44
00:02:28,941 --> 00:02:30,523
Lint does warn about that,

45
00:02:30,973 --> 00:02:32,737
and I'll show you the warning at the end,

46
00:02:33,187 --> 00:02:35,175
because it comes with a trap.

47
00:02:36,075 --> 00:02:39,849
Now, this line is new: Starts when, revealed.

48
00:02:40,749 --> 00:02:45,064
It means this step is hidden and asleep, until something wakes it.

49
00:02:45,964 --> 00:02:48,244
The Quest Log doesn't list it at all,

50
00:02:48,694 --> 00:02:51,271
it only says that more is to follow.

51
00:02:52,471 --> 00:02:55,587
Nothing wakes it yet, and lint knows that.

52
00:02:56,487 --> 00:02:58,155
It read the word revealed,

53
00:02:58,605 --> 00:03:02,207
went looking for the line that reveals this step, and found none.

54
00:03:03,107 --> 00:03:05,096
Now read to the end of the warning,

55
00:03:05,546 --> 00:03:07,735
because it writes the line out for me,

56
00:03:08,185 --> 00:03:11,454
and the line begins Then, reveal.

57
00:03:12,354 --> 00:03:15,933
That says, when Close Inspection finishes, start that one.

58
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:20,806
Notice it's the full address, arc, slash, step,

59
00:03:21,256 --> 00:03:22,903
and not just the word home.

60
00:03:23,803 --> 00:03:27,248
One Then line is all this step needs.

61
00:03:29,048 --> 00:03:31,906
So I add it, I save, and lint says clean.

62
00:03:32,806 --> 00:03:36,126
That's a chain: you finish one, and the next begins.

63
00:03:37,026 --> 00:03:40,085
In the Quest Log, Bring the Log Home appears

64
00:03:40,535 --> 00:03:43,138
the moment Close Inspection shows Done.

65
00:03:44,338 --> 00:03:49,035
Next comes a bonus: reach the hulk inside two minutes.

66
00:03:49,935 --> 00:03:53,735
In the Quest Log, it's the step with its own clock under it.

67
00:03:54,635 --> 00:03:56,323
It has a Done when line,

68
00:03:56,773 --> 00:03:59,450
and it has the opposite, Fails when,

69
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,038
and whichever comes first decides it.

70
00:04:02,938 --> 00:04:05,156
So if the crew is quick, they're paid fifty.

71
00:04:05,606 --> 00:04:07,608
If they're slow, the step fails,

72
00:04:08,058 --> 00:04:09,315
and that's all that happens.

73
00:04:10,515 --> 00:04:14,849
As it stands, the story waits for every step, the bonus included.

74
00:04:15,749 --> 00:04:19,294
So if the bonus failed, the story could never finish.

75
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:22,832
That's why I say which steps count.

76
00:04:23,732 --> 00:04:28,458
I add two lines, Part of salvage, and Required true,

77
00:04:28,908 --> 00:04:31,723
on these two steps, and not on the bonus.

78
00:04:32,623 --> 00:04:34,257
And now the story is done

79
00:04:34,707 --> 00:04:36,243
when the required steps are done.

80
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:39,504
There are two arcs in this file,

81
00:04:39,954 --> 00:04:42,030
and they start with the same three lines,

82
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,309
so I make sure I'm in Salvage Run.

83
00:04:45,209 --> 00:04:46,863
First comes a time limit,

84
00:04:47,313 --> 00:04:51,692
and that's the clock the crew sees under Salvage Run in the Quest Log.

85
00:04:53,492 --> 00:04:55,920
Then come the two endings, one each way.

86
00:04:56,820 --> 00:05:00,811
When the game ends, it ends on this screen, Game results,

87
00:05:01,261 --> 00:05:03,922
and the sentence near the top is mine.

88
00:05:04,822 --> 00:05:07,460
In the file they're Win, with a sentence,

89
00:05:07,910 --> 00:05:10,061
and Lose, with a sentence.

90
00:05:10,961 --> 00:05:13,634
Win fires when this record is finished,

91
00:05:14,084 --> 00:05:16,379
and Lose fires when it fails.

92
00:05:18,179 --> 00:05:19,566
And here's the rule to remember:

93
00:05:20,016 --> 00:05:22,088
Fails when only fails a quest.

94
00:05:22,988 --> 00:05:25,751
It's Lose that makes a failure end the game.

95
00:05:27,551 --> 00:05:29,560
So I run lint, and it's clean.

96
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:33,511
Now, there's one mistake I want you to see

97
00:05:33,961 --> 00:05:35,530
before you make it yourself:

98
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,977
one hash too few on a step.

99
00:05:38,877 --> 00:05:43,114
Lint warns me, and it's talking about line seventy-three,

100
00:05:43,564 --> 00:05:46,429
which is my Then line, and not the heading I changed.

101
00:05:47,329 --> 00:05:49,685
You know that habit of lint's from Lecture 6.

102
00:05:50,585 --> 00:05:52,494
But look at how the sentence ends.

103
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:55,657
It's found my step in its new place,

104
00:05:56,107 --> 00:05:58,857
and it offers me a new Then line that points there.

105
00:05:59,757 --> 00:06:01,973
If I write that, lint says clean,

106
00:06:02,423 --> 00:06:05,613
and the game is won the moment the crew reaches the hulk,

107
00:06:06,063 --> 00:06:08,757
because my story has only one step left.

108
00:06:10,557 --> 00:06:13,161
The Then line was right all along,

109
00:06:13,611 --> 00:06:15,652
and it was the heading that was wrong.

110
00:06:16,552 --> 00:06:20,049
So, when lint offers you a new Then line,

111
00:06:20,499 --> 00:06:22,425
count the hashes on the step first.

112
00:06:23,625 --> 00:06:26,094
Here's the Quest Log, with two steps showing,

113
00:06:26,544 --> 00:06:28,138
and the third one still hidden.

114
00:06:29,038 --> 00:06:31,096
So in we go, toward the hulk.

115
00:06:31,996 --> 00:06:35,226
Helm says Quest complete, Quick Work,

116
00:06:35,676 --> 00:06:37,775
and Close Inspection is done with it.

117
00:06:38,675 --> 00:06:42,977
And there's step three in the Quest Log, Bring the Log Home,

118
00:06:43,427 --> 00:06:44,761
so we turn for home.

119
00:06:45,661 --> 00:06:48,167
And that's the end screen, Game results,

120
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:49,995
with my Win sentence on it.

121
00:06:51,195 --> 00:06:53,843
Now I change ten minutes to thirty seconds,

122
00:06:54,293 --> 00:06:55,831
and I sit on my hands.

123
00:06:56,731 --> 00:06:58,192
And there's the end screen again,

124
00:06:58,642 --> 00:07:01,247
this time with my Lose sentence on it.

125
00:07:02,148 --> 00:07:03,942
Notice that nobody warned me.

126
00:07:04,842 --> 00:07:08,116
The only countdown is that clock in the Quest Log,

127
00:07:08,566 --> 00:07:10,477
so tell the crew the limit,

128
00:07:10,927 --> 00:07:13,578
the way my table does in the arc's briefing,

129
00:07:14,028 --> 00:07:16,329
and tell them again in the first step's.

130
00:07:17,229 --> 00:07:19,168
And then I put ten minutes back.

131
00:07:20,368 --> 00:07:22,106
Now it's your turn: add a fourth step.

132
00:07:23,006 --> 00:07:24,573
It's revealed by the third,

133
00:07:25,023 --> 00:07:27,462
it's finished by a timer, and it's required.

134
00:07:28,362 --> 00:07:31,486
Then the win comes thirty seconds after they get home.

135
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:36,329
Next time, we look at the things quests point at.
